{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Sits at the top of a patch track FX chain and decides whether new notes reach the instrument below. Never blocks note-offs; flushes held notes + CC64 on close. Superseded by Note Tracker & Input Gate for StageRig, kept for simple rigs.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs40 Nathaniel Tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Dockable ReaImGui apps and a keyboard speed layer for REAPER, built by a working producer for his own sessions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Jason Zac} \u183? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nathanielschool.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul Nathaniel School of Music}}} \u183? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://daw.nathanielschool.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul daw.nathanielschool.com}}}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 \i These exist because his own sessions were slow, not because anyone surveyed a market.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 \i Every app in here replaces a REAPER custom action that was quietly doing the wrong thing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Status:} 68 automated checks passing, 0 failing, against REAPER 7.77 on macOS arm64.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 What's in it\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 Apps (dockable, ReaImGui, one accent colour each)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 App  \u8212?  Colour  \u8212?  What it does\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Folders & Flow}  \u8212?  green  \u8212?  Fix, build, dissolve, move and isolate track folders. Repairs a session whose folder maths has gone wrong.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Palette & Look}  \u8212?  violet  \u8212?  Colour and name tracks from {\i meaning} \u8212? rules, palettes, families, live watcher.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Track Settings Transfer}  \u8212?  violet  \u8212?  Pro-Tools style "Import Session Data" across project tabs, in both directions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b Stem Print & Handoff}  \u8212?  amber  \u8212?  Print stems in several modes and restore the session exactly afterwards.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 {\b MIDI Batch Export}  \u8212?  amber  \u8212?  Export many MIDI items/regions as separate {\f1 .mid} files with pattern-based sequential names.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 The speed layer (12 scripts, keyboard-bound)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Solo Focus \u183? Record Arm Toggle \u183? FX Float Toggle \u183? FX Open/Close All \u183? Region Next/Prev \u183? Marker at Bar \u183? Tempo at Bar \u183? MIDI Render \u183? Flush Paste \u183? Duplicate Track \u183? Unsolo & Unselect\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each one replaced a custom action that had a real, diagnosed bug \u8212? a pan-destroying step, a global preference being toggled on every press, a marker snapping to the arrange grid instead of the bar line. The root causes are documented in {\f1 docs/TECH_BRIEF.md}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 The shared spine\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab {\b `scripts/lib/nt_safe.lua`} \u8212? pointer safety and stable identity. The reason these apps\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 cannot crash REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab {\b `scripts/lib/nt_hierarchy.lua`} \u8212? folder maths. Converts REAPER's {\f1 I_FOLDERDEPTH} integers\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 to nesting levels, edits there, and regenerates. Well-formed output by construction.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Two things that make this different from a folder of scripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 1. It cannot crash REAPER\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER frees a {\f1 MediaTrack*} the instant the track is deleted. Handing a freed pointer to any REAPER API faults inside REAPER's own C++, and {\b Lua `pcall` cannot catch it} \u8212? the host process dies, taking unsaved projects with it. Wrapping your draw loop in {\f1 pcall} is false comfort.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Every app here stores {\b track GUIDs}, resolves them to pointers immediately before use, validates with {\f1 ValidatePtr2}, and never holds a pointer across a defer frame. The test suite deletes a track behind an app's back and asserts that every accessor returns a clean default instead of faulting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 2. Folder edits are well-formed by construction\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Folder scripts go wrong because they edit {\f1 I_FOLDERDEPTH} in place: a local edit that looks right leaves the arithmetic unbalanced further down, and REAPER silently swallows the rest of the session into a folder.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 nt_hierarchy} never edits depths. It converts to levels, edits there, and regenerates every depth. The output always balances \u8212? it is not possible for the app to leave a folder hanging open.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires {\b [ReaImGui](https://github.com/cfillion/reaimgui)} and {\b [SWS](https://sws-extension.org)}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 With ReaPack (recommended)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository {\b is} a ReaPack repository. In REAPER:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tab {\b Extensions \u8594? ReaPack \u8594? Import repositories\u8230?}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tab Paste this URL and click OK:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 https://github.com/jasonzacmusic/nathaniel-tools/raw/main/index.xml}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tab {\b Extensions \u8594? ReaPack \u8594? Browse packages\u8230?}, filter on {\f1 Nathaniel Tools}, and install what you want.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Every package is signed with a SHA-256 checksum and every download is pinned to a git commit, so an installed version can never change underneath you. Updates arrive through {\b Extensions \u8594? ReaPack \u8594? Synchronize packages}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs32 By hand\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tab Copy {\f1 scripts/} and {\f1 apps/} somewhere REAPER can see them.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tab {\i Actions \u8594? Show action list \u8594? New action\u8230? \u8594? Load ReaScript}, and pick each app.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tab Or run {\f1 tests/harness.lua} once \u8212? it registers everything for you and verifies the install.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Publishing (maintainer notes)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 index.xml} at the repository root is the ReaPack index. It is rebuilt automatically by {\f1 .github/workflows/reapack.yml} on every push to {\f1 main}, and can be rebuilt by hand:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 python3 tools/build_index.py --check   # validate headers, write nothing}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 python3 tools/build_index.py           # rebuild index.xml}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 tools/build_index.py} is a dependency-free implementation of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://codeberg.org/cfillion/reapack/wiki/Index-Format"}}{\fldrslt{\ul ReaPack Index Format}}} \u8212? Python 3 and {\f1 git}, nothing else, and byte-identical output on any machine. CI also runs cfillion's own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul `reapack-index`}}} in {\f1 --check} mode as a second opinion on the headers.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Two rules for anything new that lands in {\f1 scripts/} or {\f1 apps/}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab Every {\f1 .lua} / {\f1 .jsfx} file needs a metadata header with at least {\f1 @version}, or it\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 fails the build. See the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index/wiki/Packaging-Documentation"}}{\fldrslt{\ul Packaging Documentation}}}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 \u8226 ?\tab Shared libraries carry {\f1 @noindex} and are listed in the {\f1 @provides} of the script that\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 needs them, so they install alongside it instead of appearing as their own package.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Files must live in a subdirectory \u8212? ReaPack never indexes files at the repository root, and the directory name becomes the category shown in ReaPack.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Testing\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 lua tests/hierarchy_test.lua      # 31 checks, no REAPER needed}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Inside REAPER, run {\f1 tests/harness.lua} from the action list \u8212? 68 checks including live crash-safety. It builds its scratch project {\b in its own tab} and closes it afterwards, so it never touches the project you had open. Results land in {\f1 _nt_results.txt}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \li360 \i Edit {\f1 BASE} at the top of {\f1 harness.lua} to point at your install path.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Two REAPER API traps documented here\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Both cost real debugging time. Neither is in the official docs.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tab {\b `GetProjectStateChangeCount` does not detect track changes.} Measured in 7.77: it\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 stayed on {\f1 8} across insert, rename {\i and} delete. Any change-watchdog built on it never fires. Use a track-list signature instead.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa60 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tab {\b `ValidatePtr2` rejects `0`} \u8212? even though {\f1 0} is ReaScript's shorthand for "the\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 current project". Guards must special-case it or they return false for everything.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 More in {\f1 docs/TECH_BRIEF.md}.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs36 Licence\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIT \u8212? see {\f1 LICENSE}.\par}
}
